  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 6 and takes 15 minutes to prepare, then needs at least 8 hours in the freezer. It is a"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "no-churn"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "ice cream, so no machine is needed. The result is smooth, creamy and deeply flavoured with"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "matcha"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use good-quality ceremonial or culinary grade matcha. Cheaper matcha can taste bitter or muddy. Mix the matcha to a smooth paste with a small amount of the condensed milk before adding to the cream. This prevents lumps and distributes the flavour evenly."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 4,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "double-cream",
              "amount": 600,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": "very cold",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "condensed-milk",
              "amount": 397,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "one standard tin",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "matcha-powder",
              "amount": 3,
              "unit": "tbsp",
              "prepNote": "sifted",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Sift the matcha powder into a small bowl. Add 2 tablespoons of the condensed milk and stir to a smooth green paste. Set aside."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour the cold"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "double cream"
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "into a large bowl. Whisk with the electric hand whisk until it holds soft peaks. Do not overwhip."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Stir the matcha paste into the remaining condensed milk until fully combined."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour the matcha condensed milk into the whipped cream. Fold together gently with a spatula until the mixture is an even pale green with no streaks."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Pour into a freezer-safe container. Smooth the top. Cover with a lid or cling film pressed directly onto the surface."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Freeze for at least 8 hours or overnight. Remove from the freezer 5 minutes before serving to soften slightly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "attrs": {
          "items": [
            {
              "symptom": "Ice cream is icy rather than creamy",
              "cause": "The cream was not whipped enough before folding in the condensed milk.",
              "fix": "Whip to soft peaks next time. The air in the cream keeps the texture smooth as it freezes."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Matcha lumps in the finished ice cream",
              "cause": "The matcha was added directly without making a paste first.",
              "fix": "Always mix matcha with a small amount of liquid to a smooth paste before adding to the batch. Sifting also helps."
            },
            {
              "symptom": "Flavour is bitter",
              "cause": "Too much matcha was used or the matcha quality is low.",
              "fix": "Start with 2 tablespoons next time and taste the mixture before freezing. Higher-grade matcha is less bitter."
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Matcha ice cream is one of the most recognisable Japanese desserts outside Japan. It is sold in ice cream parlours, vending machines, convenience stores and tea shops across the country. Matcha has been used in Japanese tea ceremonies for centuries. Using it in ice cream became popular in the twentieth century. The vivid green colour and slightly bitter, grassy flavour make it unlike any other ice cream."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}